\f0\fs24 \cf0 Data notes:\
Behavioral data for all patients is stored in the \'91behaviorData/*_behavior\'92 file (* indicates the task). For the first several sessions, patients completed 550 trials without interruption. Starting from patient 16WV, 555 trials were completed as we added 5 more one-back trials. In some sessions, a few trials were removed manually due to interruptions. 
\f1 \

\f0 The variable \'91sessions\'92 contains the header information of each session, corresponding to the order in behavioral data.\
The timing parameters for each trial can be found in the variable \'91iT\'92. Stimulus presentation order is in the variable \'91code\'92, which contains the index for each face image. Indices for the repeated (i.e., one-back) trials are stored in the variable \'91back_id\'92. If the patient responded (i.e., pressed the space bar) in the one-back trial, the value is 1 for this trial in the variable \'91vResp\'92; otherwise, the value is 0. Response time is stored in the variable \'91RT\'92.\
\
Data usage:\
Please see \'91SingleNeuron/Code/SortFR.m\'92 for an example to extract and use the behavior data. }